George Gershwin died on July 11, 1937, at the age of 38, due to complications from a brain tumor. He was buried at Westchester Hills Cemetery in Harrison, New York.

There is a notable monument dedicated to his memory: the George Gershwin Memorial, located in Central Park, New York City. The memorial features a bronze plaque and a bust of Gershwin, and is situated near the Bethesda Fountain.

Additionally, the Gershwin Theatre, a Broadway theater in New York City, is named in his honor.
